---
permalink: /assets/favicons/site.webmanifest
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#- The manifest is rendered, not copied. As static JSON it drifted: it shipped
    with the favicon generator's empty name/short_name and a stock theme colour,
    and nothing on the page reveals either — they only surface once someone
    installs the site or adds it to an Android home screen.

    name/short_name follow client.js, and both colours are the page ground
    (secondary-700, the same value base.njk hands to <meta name="theme-color">),
    so an installed app cannot flash a white frame the site never uses.

    icons[].src stay RELATIVE: a leading slash 404s under a preview build's
    subfolder. -#}
{
  {#- `| dump` writes the JSON string INCLUDING its quotes. Interpolating into
      hand-written quotes instead runs the value through Nunjucks' autoescaper,
      which is an HTML escaper — and a .webmanifest is raw text, so a name
      containing "&" reaches an Android home screen as "Foo &amp; Bar". Nothing
      on the page reveals it. -#}
  "name": {{ (client.restaurantName or client.name) | dump | safe }},
  "short_name": {{ (client.shortName or client.name) | dump | safe }},
  "icons": [
    {
      "src": "android-chrome-192x192.png",
      "sizes": "192x192",
      "type": "image/png"
    },
    {
      "src": "android-chrome-512x512.png",
      "sizes": "512x512",
      "type": "image/png"
    }
  ],
  "theme_color": "{{ theme.colors.secondary['700'] }}",
  "background_color": "{{ theme.colors.secondary['700'] }}",
  "display": "standalone"
}
